 and division by zero is undefined.\n\nNow, multiplying both sides of the equation by the least common denominator, we can simplify it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{T-3}+\\frac{5}{T-4}-\\frac{5}{(T-3)(T-4)} & =0 \\\\ (T-3)(T-4)\\cdot (\\frac{2}{T-3}+\\frac{5}{T-4}-\\frac{5}{(T-3)(T-4)}) & =(T-3)(T-4)\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{2(T-3)(T-4)}{T-3}+\\frac{5(T-3)(T-4)}{T-4}-\\frac{5(T-3)(T-4)}{(T-3)(T-4)} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{(T-3)}(T-4)}{\\cancel{T-3}}+\\frac{5(T-3)\\cdot \\cancel{(T-4)}}{\\cancel{T-4}}-\\frac{5\\cdot \\cancel{(T-3)(T-4)}}{\\cancel{(T-3)(T-4)}} & =0 \\\\ 2(T-4)+5(T-3)-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSolving this equation for $T,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(T-4)+5(T-3)-5 & =0 \\\\ 2T-8+5T-15-5 & =0 \\\\ 7T & =28 \\\\ T & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nHowever, since $T=4$ is not a valid solution, our equation has no solutions." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
